{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tuning system based on just intonation, using exact integer frequency ratios."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"externalID":"s:10IvorTuning14JustIntonationV","title":"JustIntonation","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"JustIntonation"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"JustIntonation"}]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/init(ratios:equivalenceRatio:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/equivalenceRatio","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/ratios"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/TuningSystem-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"JustIntonation"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/UsingIvorTuning"]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A just intonation system is defined by a set of frequency ratios relative to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tonic, each derived from small-integer harmonics. Any number of tones per interval of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equivalence is supported — from a simple pentatonic to Harry Partch’s 43-tone 11-limit scale."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On initialization, ratios outside ","type":"text"},{"code":"[1, equivalenceRatio)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are reduced by dividing by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"equivalenceRatio","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" until they fall in range; exact multiples of ","type":"text"},{"code":"equivalenceRatio","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(including 1:1) are silently discarded. The remaining ratios are deduplicated and sorted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ascending.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/JustIntonation\/ratios","type":"reference"},{"text":" property prepends the tonic (1:1) and appends the interval of equivalence,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so it always spans one complete interval of equivalence.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does not support standard pitch notation. Just intonation systems are too variable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to map reliably to the 35 pitch classes of standard notation: even 5-limit scales"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contain enharmonic pairs that are distinct in just intonation but share a single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spelling, and higher-limit systems diverge further or exceed the 35-pitch-class maximum."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"va